<h3 id="awards">Awards</h2>

<p>Enya's critical acclaim is anchored by <strong>four Grammy Awards</strong>, all won in the <em>Best New Age Album</em> category:</p>

<ul>
    <li><strong>1993:</strong> Won for <a href="/shepherd-moons/"><em>Shepherd Moons</em></a>.</li>
    <li><strong>1997:</strong> Won for <a href="/the-memory-of-trees/"><em>The Memory of Trees</em></a>.</li>
    <li><strong>2002:</strong> Won for <a href="/a-day-without-rain/"><em>A Day Without Rain</em></a>.</li>
    <li><strong>2007:</strong> Won for <a href="/enya-amarantine/"><em>Amarantine</em></a>.</li>
</ul>

<p>Her cinematic work has also drawn major award attention.</p> 

<p>Her song <a href="/enya-other/#May_It_Be">"May It Be"</a> for <a href="/the-lord-of-the-rings/"><em>The Lord Of The Rings - The Fellowship Of The Ring</em></a> received dual nominations for a Golden Globe and an <strong>Academy Award for Best Original Song</strong> in 2002.</p>

<p>Other major industry accolades include:</p>
<ul>
    <li><strong>IRMA Awards:</strong> Named "Best Female Irish Artist" in 1989 and 1993.</li>
    <li><strong>World Music Awards:</strong> Captured five distinct trophies, including "Best Solo Irish Artist", "Best New Age Artist", and "Best-selling Female Artist" across the 2001, 2002, and 2006 ceremonies.</li>
    <li><strong>BRIT Awards:</strong> Enya holds the record as the most-nominated female Irish artist in BRIT history, with four nominations.</li>
</ul>

