<h4>Who is "Eithne"? How to pronounce "Eithne"?</h4>

<p><strong>Eithne</strong> is Enya's birth name.</p> 

<p>"Enya" is simply the phonetic spelling of "Eithne," which is pronounced as <strong>ehn-ya</strong>.</p> 

<p>When she began her solo career, she chose to adapt the spelling to avoid constant mispronunciations by non-Gaelic speakers.</p>

<h4>Why do some people use Eithne and not Enya?</h4>

<p>Fans generally use <strong>Eithne</strong> when referring to the individual woman.</p> 

<p>The name <strong>Enya</strong> is used to represent the musical entity created by the collaborative trio: Eithne Brennan, Nicky Ryan (1946-2025), and Roma Ryan.</p>

<h4>Who are Roma and Nicky Ryan?</h4>

<p><a href="/roma-ryan-nicky/">Nicky and Roma</a> formed the production and management team behind Enya's massive solo success.</p> 

<p>Nicky Ryan (1946-2025) acted as her producer, arranger, and manager, while Roma is her exclusive lyricist.</p> 

<p>Nicky originally served as the sound engineer and manager for the family band <a href="/enya-clannad/">Clannad</a> before breaking away to focus on Enya's solo career.</p>

<h4>Who is Clannad and what relationship do they have with Enya?</h4>

<p><a href="/enya-clannad/">Clannad</a> is a globally successful Irish folk band composed entirely of Enya's family members.</p> 

<p>The core lineup features her twin uncles, Noel and Pádraig Duggan, alongside her older siblings Ciarán, Pól, and Máire (Moya) Brennan.</p>

<h4>Who is Moya Brennan and what relationship does she have with Enya?</h4>

<p>Moya (born Máire) is Enya's eldest sister.</p> 

<p>She serves as the lead vocalist and harpist for Clannad and has maintained a highly successful solo career of her own.</p>

<h4>Who is Aigle?</h4>

<p><strong>Aigle</strong> (the French word for "Eagle") is the name of Enya's private recording studio.</p> 

<p>It also functions as the umbrella name for the business entity operated by Enya, Roma, and Nicky Ryan.</p>

<h4>What colour are Enya's eyes?</h4>

<p>Enya's eye color appears to shift between green, hazel, and grey depending on the lighting in different photos or music videos.</p> 

<p>While she may occasionally use colored lenses for stylized shoots, most fans agree her natural color is a striking hazel-grey.</p>

<h4>What is her address?</h4>

<p>Enya maintains fierce privacy regarding her personal residence at Manderley Castle.</p> 

<p>Direct fan mail should not be sent to her home. Fans can send letters through her official label representation:</p>

<p>Enya<br />
c/o Warner Music Ireland<br />
22 South Great George's Street<br />
Dublin 2<br />
Ireland</p>

<h4>Enya looks so beautiful! How does she manage that? Does she have a special diet?</h4>

<p>Most widely circulated photos of Enya are highly produced promotional shots for magazines or album booklets.</p> 

<p>Like any major artist, she works with professional makeup and lighting teams.</p> 

<p>As for her lifestyle, she eats a very clean diet consisting mostly of fish and vegetables, avoids red meat, and occasionally enjoys a glass of dry white wine.</p>

<h4>Does Enya really do all the instruments and vocals herself?</h4>

<p>Yes, Enya provides the vast majority of the instrumentation and layers all of her own vocals.</p> 

<p>While she primarily focuses on the piano and synthesizers, she also performs string and percussion parts.</p>

<h4>Is all the music on Enya's albums composed only by her?</h4>

<p>Enya composes almost all of her original music.</p> 

<p>Throughout her multi-decade career, she has only recorded a handful of traditional arrangements.</p> 

<p>These include <a href="/shepherd-moons/#Marble_Halls">"Marble Halls"</a> (from an 1843 opera), <a href="/shepherd-moons/#How_Can_I_Keep_From_Singing">"How Can I Keep from Singing?"</a> (a Shaker hymn), and classic Christmas carols like <a href="/enya-other/#Oiche_Chiun">"Oiche Chiun"</a> and <a href="/enya-other/#Adeste_Fideles">"Adeste, Fideles"</a>.</p>

<h4>Some of Enya's songs are not in English, what language are they?</h4>

<p>Enya has recorded vocals in an astonishing <strong>ten different languages</strong>.</p> 

<p>These include English, Irish Gaelic, Latin, Spanish, Japanese, Welsh, and French.</p> 

<p>She has also sung in three fictional languages: J.R.R. Tolkien's <strong>Quenya</strong> and <strong>Sindarin</strong>, and Roma Ryan's <strong>Loxian</strong>.</p>

<ul>
    <li><strong>Irish Gaelic</strong>: "March of the Celts", "Aldebaran", "Deireadh An Tuath", "Storms In Africa", "Oiche Chiun", "Ebudae", "Book of Days", "Smaointe", "Athair Ar Neamh", "Deora Ar Mo Chroi"</li>
    <li><strong>French</strong>: Featured in "Only If"</li>
    <li><strong>Japanese</strong>: "Sumiregusa"</li>
    <li><strong>Latin</strong>: "Cursum Perficio", "Afer Ventus", "Pax Deorum", "Tempus Vernum", "Adeste, Fideles"</li>
    <li><strong>Spanish</strong>: "La Sonadora"</li>
    <li><strong>Welsh</strong>: "Dan y Dwr"</li>
    <li><strong>Sindarin</strong>: "Aniron"</li>
    <li><strong>Quenya</strong>: Featured in "May It Be"</li>
    <li><strong>Loxian</strong>: "Less Than A Pearl", "The River Sings", "Water Shows The Hidden Heart"</li>
</ul>

<h4>What is Loxian?</h4>

<p><strong>Loxian</strong> is a fully constructed fictional language created by lyricist <strong>Roma Ryan</strong>.</p> 

<p>She invented the language specifically for Enya's 2005 album, <em>Amarantine</em>, when standard English or Gaelic phrasing failed to capture the necessary musical mood.</p> 

<p>Inspired by Tolkien's Elvish languages, Roma expanded Loxian into a published book titled <em>Water Shows the Hidden Heart</em>.</p>

<h4>Was that Enya I heard? Is this song really an Enya song?</h4>

<p>Because Enya's style is heavily imitated, peer-to-peer sharing networks frequently mislabel ethereal songs as her work.</p> 

<p>Tracks like "Now We Are Free" (from Gladiator), "Harry's Game" (actually by Clannad), and "Return to Innocence" (by Enigma) are constantly, and incorrectly, attributed to Enya.</p> 

<p>Always cross-reference a <a href="/all-enya-songs/">complete list of Enya songs</a> to verify authenticity.</p>

<h4>How many records has she sold?</h4>

<p>Enya is one of the most successful female artists in history, selling over <strong>80 million albums worldwide</strong>.</p> 

<p>Her zenith was the 2000 release <a href="/a-day-without-rain/"><em>A Day Without Rain</em></a>, which sold an estimated <strong>16 million copies</strong> globally.</p>

